window.STUDY={"id":"ap-29-session-docket","code":"AP-29","title":"Session docket · a conversation, typed","fig":"4.29","kicker":"Application · 29","lede":"A Mindgut session as a typed docket.","body":["Each turn carries the product's left rule: --c147 blue for the person (.msg.user) and --c258 purple for Mir (.msg.assistant). The rule is struck through the colored half of the ribbon, one bar per line. Times, the turn count and the duration are typed from the session itself, and one slip is struck out with x's. The session is fictional and the text is invented."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Typewriter strike, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":2250},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"c-transcript","job":"concept","title":"Session docket · a conversation, typed","aspect":"2/3","uses":["fx-07-typewriter","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"A Mindgut session as a typed docket. Each turn carries the product's left rule: --c147 blue for the person (.msg.user) and --c258 purple for Mir (.msg.assistant). The rule is struck through the colored half of the ribbon, one bar per line. Times, the turn count and the duration are typed from the session itself, and one slip is struck out with x's. The session is fictional and the text is invented."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-07-typewriter","name":"Typewriter strike","short":"FX-07","atoms":["transfer","deform"],"params":{"fsize":{"value":34,"range":[8,48],"label":"Size","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"type size in CSS px; bold below 15 px"},"lead":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,2.4],"label":"Leading","step":0.01,"note":"line spacing as a multiple of the size"},"vari":{"value":0.28,"range":[0,1],"label":"Key variance","step":0.01,"note":"how unevenly keys strike"},"half":{"value":0.07,"range":[0,0.4],"label":"Half strikes","step":0.005,"note":"share of glyphs where only the top or bottom lands"},"jx":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter x","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"horizontal offset per strike"},"jy":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter y","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"vertical offset per strike"},"rot":{"value":0.6,"range":[0,4],"label":"Rotation","step":0.05,"unit":"°","note":"rotation spread per strike"},"exhaust":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon wear","step":0.01,"note":"ink fading along the text"},"ribbon":{"value":0.62,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon texture","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ribbon weave shows in the glyphs"},"rcount":{"value":95,"range":[20,200],"label":"Ribbon count","step":1,"unit":"/100px","note":"ribbon threads per 100 CSS px"},"squash":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink squash","step":0.01,"note":"film pooling at the glyph edge"},"impress":{"value":0.32,"range":[0,1],"label":"Press depth","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how deep each strike dents the stock"},"diffuse":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"bite":{"value":0.55,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":0.85,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.12,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":0.8,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.006,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert)"},"seed":{"value":17,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Text in Courier Prime (a typewriter slab; bold below 15 px, as a light strike loses thin strokes), one strike per glyph on the main thread: pressure = ribbon life (exhausting along the page) × key variance; offset, rotation, an occasional dropped baseline; a half strike is a linear pressure ramp across the glyph, fading top or bottom. Ribbon: a plain weave at the ribbon count. Ink transfers through thread crossings, less through the gaps. Ink chain: pressure × ribbon vs stock-height percentile; ink squash pools film at the glyph edge. Impression: the strike dents the stock (blurred glyph × pressure); light from the combined height. Color: Beer–Lambert film.","limits":"ribbon count < 30 /100 px: weave reads as a screen pattern on the type. jitter > 1.5 px: reads as broken font rendering. size < 7 px: strokes thinner than the tooth lose the ribbon texture"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":3,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":1.6,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.4,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.6,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.035,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.014,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Typewriter strike · Each glyph is a separate strike: its own pressure, a slight offset and rotation, sometimes only half the face lands.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
